{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-evap-leaks fixture",
    "description": "The `process-evap-leaks` fixture: the run's EXECUTION database -- the snapshot's own tables, cut from the default database for this RunSpec and holding its generators' intermediate tables -- mounted on `onroad/model.esm`. It holds no logic: its `data_sources` are the catalogue under the names the model reads, and its one `{ref}` binds the run's declared counts. run-tests.sh's fixture stage emits the model's `out_*` relation and compares it with the snapshot's MOVESOutput; a mounted model's inline tests do not run (finding F47), so that comparison is its whole check. `runspecs/process-evap-leaks.esm` reproduces the same run from the DEFAULT database through the same model, so the pair is a differential test of the execution-database cut: one model, one oracle, two catalogues.\n\nUntil 2026-10-30 this file inlined its own copy of the onroad model (1809 lines, frozen at the commit that last touched it), so the logic every fixture shared was written fourteen times. PLAN.md §7.1, docs/esm-conventions.md §106."
  },
